{
  "_comment": "The start menu, and the first half of the scene-change demo. Three entities: the GameController that owns the fade and survives the load as static state, a title, and a button. The button's StartMenu script asks the controller to open scenes/collector.oscene; it never calls RequestScene itself, which is the whole point of routing every scene change through one object.",
  "_fade": "There is no fade overlay entity in this file on purpose. GameController builds its own in OnStart, so adding the controller to a level is one entity rather than two - and so nobody can save a level with the overlay left opaque.",
